{
  "title": "Tutorial: Get started with Go",
  "description": "In this tutorial, you'll get a brief introduction to Go programming. Along the way, you will:",
  "body": {
    "type": "document",
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "id": null,
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Tutorial: Get started with Go"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "anchor",
        "id": "nav"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "In this tutorial, you'll get a brief introduction to Go programming. Along the way, you will:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "start": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Install Go (if you haven't already)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Write some simple \"Hello, world\" code."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Use the "
              },
              {
                "type": "inline_code",
                "code": "go"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " command to run your code."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Use the Go package discovery tool to find packages you can use in your own code."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Call functions of an external module."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "prerequisites",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Prerequisites"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "start": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Some programming experience."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " The code here is pretty simple, but it helps to know something about functions."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "A tool to edit your code."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " Any text editor you have will work fine. Most text editors have good support for Go. The most popular are VSCode (free), GoLand (paid), and Vim (free)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "A command terminal."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " Go works well using any terminal on Linux and Mac, and on PowerShell or cmd in Windows."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "install",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Install Go"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Just use the "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/doc/install",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Download and install"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " steps."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "code",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Write some code"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Get started with Hello, World."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "start": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Open a command prompt and cd to your home directory. "
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "On Linux or Mac:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "cd"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "On Windows:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "cd %HOMEPATH%"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Create a hello directory for your first Go source code. "
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "For example, use the following commands:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "mkdir hello\ncd hello"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Enable dependency tracking for your code. "
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "When your code imports packages contained in other modules, you manage those dependencies through your code's own module. That module is defined by a go.mod file that tracks the modules that provide those packages. That go.mod file stays with your code, including in your source code repository."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "To enable dependency tracking for your code by creating a go.mod file, run the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://corpus.test/ref/mod#go-mod-init",
                    "title": null,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "go mod init"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " command, giving it the name of the module your code will be in. The name is the module's module path."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "In actual development, the module path will typically be the repository location where your source code will be kept. For example, the module path might be "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "github.com/mymodule"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": ". If you plan to publish your module for others to use, the module path "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "emphasis",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "must"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " be a location from which Go tools can download your module. For more about naming a module with a module path, see "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://corpus.test/doc/modules/managing-dependencies#naming_module",
                    "title": null,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Managing dependencies"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "For the purposes of this tutorial, just use "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "example/hello"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "$ go mod init example/hello\ngo: creating new go.mod: module example/hello"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "In your text editor, create a file hello.go in which to write your code."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Paste the following code into your hello.go file and save the file."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello, World!\")\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "This is your Go code. In this code, you:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "start": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Declare a "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "main"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " package (a package is a way to group functions, and it's made up of all the files in the same directory)."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Import the popular "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/fmt/",
                        "title": null,
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "inline_code",
                            "code": "fmt"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": " package"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": ", which contains functions for formatting text, including printing to the console. This package is one of the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/std",
                        "title": null,
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": "standard library"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " packages you got when you installed Go."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Implement a "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "main"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " function to print a message to the console. A "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "main"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " function executes by default when you run the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "main"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " package."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Run your code to see the greeting."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "$ go run .\nHello, World!"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://corpus.test/cmd/go/#hdr-Compile_and_run_Go_program",
                    "title": null,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "go run"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " command is one of many "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "go"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " commands you'll use to get things done with Go. Use the following command to get a list of the others:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "$ go help"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "call",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Call code in an external package"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "When you need your code to do something that might have been implemented by someone else, you can look for a package that has functions you can use in your code."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "start": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Make your printed message a little more interesting with a function from an external module. "
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": true,
                "start": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Visit pkg.go.dev and "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/search?q=quote",
                        "title": null,
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": "search for a \"quote\" package"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "In the search results, locate and click on the v1 of the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "rsc.io/quote"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " package (it should be listed with the \"Other major versions\" of "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "rsc.io/quote/v4"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": ")."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "In the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "strong",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": "Documentation"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " section, under "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "strong",
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": "Index"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": ", note the list of functions you can call from your code. You'll use the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "Go"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " function."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "At the top of this page, note that package "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "quote"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " is included in the "
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "inline_code",
                        "code": "rsc.io/quote"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": " module."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "You can use the pkg.go.dev site to find published modules whose packages have functions you can use in your own code. Packages are published in modules -- like "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "rsc.io/quote"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " -- where others can use them. Modules are improved with new versions over time, and you can upgrade your code to use the improved versions."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "In your Go code, import the "
              },
              {
                "type": "inline_code",
                "code": "rsc.io/quote"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " package and add a call to its "
              },
              {
                "type": "inline_code",
                "code": "Go"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " function. "
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "After adding the highlighted lines, your code should include the following:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nimport \"rsc.io/quote\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(quote.Go())\n}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Add new module requirements and sums. "
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Go will add the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "quote"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " module as a requirement, as well as a go.sum file for use in authenticating the module. For more, see "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://corpus.test/ref/mod#authenticating",
                    "title": null,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "Authenticating modules"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " in the Go Modules Reference."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "$ go mod tidy\ngo: finding module for package rsc.io/quote\ngo: found rsc.io/quote in rsc.io/quote v1.5.2"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Run your code to see the message generated by the function you're calling. "
              },
              {
                "type": "code_block",
                "language": null,
                "code": "$ go run .\nDon't communicate by sharing memory, share memory by communicating."
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Notice that your code calls the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "Go"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " function, printing a clever message about communication."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "When you ran "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "go mod tidy"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": ", it located and downloaded the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "inline_code",
                    "code": "rsc.io/quote"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": " module that contains the package you imported. By default, it downloaded the latest version -- v1.5.2."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "write-more",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Write more code"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "With this quick introduction, you got Go installed and learned some of the basics. To write some more code with another tutorial, take a look at "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/doc/tutorial/create-module.html",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Create a Go module"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
